ER DIAGRAM DESCRIPTION (PLACEHOLDER CONTENT)

Entities:

1) User
- id (PK)
- username (unique)
- password
- role (ADMIN/TEACHER)
- created_at
- updated_at

2) Student
- id (PK)
- first_name
- last_name
- email (unique)
- roll_number (unique)
- class_group
- face_encoding
- created_at
- updated_at

3) Attendance
- id (PK)
- student_id (FK -> Student.id)
- date
- time
- status (PRESENT/ABSENT)
- marked_by (AI/MANUAL)
- created_at

Relationships:
- Student (1) ---- (M) Attendance
  One student can have many attendance records.
  Each attendance record belongs to exactly one student.

- User is related functionally (not direct FK in current schema)
  Users authenticate and manage students/attendance through application logic.

Key constraints:
- Unique: users.username, students.email, students.roll_number
- Attendance uniqueness by business rule: (student_id, date)
